course: dictionary
lesson: 13056
title: Fearless
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Fearless means not afraid of anything; very brave. Look at the word inside it: fear, and -less, which means without. A fearless person is someone without fear. «The fearless firefighter ran into the smoke to save the kitten.» The smoke and the running in are the clues: she was in danger, and she was not scared.
explain: Fearless is not the same as careless. «The careless climber did not check the rope.» Careless means not paying attention, so the climber made a mistake. A fearless climber can be just as brave, but she still checks the rope before she climbs. Brave and sensible go together.
explain: Real courage is being afraid and doing the right thing anyway. «Ella was scared of the dark, but she walked to the shed to fetch the torch.» Ella was not fearless in that moment, yet she was brave. Test a word by swapping in your meaning: does «not afraid» still fit the sentence?
fact: Fearless means not afraid of anything; very brave.
fact: Fear + less = without fear. Other words with -less work the same way, such as hopeless (without hope).
fact: «Fearless» is an adjective, and you can say more fearless or most fearless.
fact: Heroes, explorers, rescuers and animals are often called fearless in stories.
fact: Being fearless is different from being careless: real courage means thinking carefully and still doing the right thing.
exercise: «The fearless firefighter ran into the smoke to save the kitten.» What does fearless mean? | Tired after a long day | *Not afraid; very brave | Very hungry | Wet through from rain
exercise: «Sam was careless and forgot to check the rope.» Is careless the same as fearless? | Yes, they mean exactly the same thing | Yes, both mean happy | No, careless means very brave | *No, careless means not paying attention, but fearless means not afraid
exercise: «The fearless explorer crossed the icy river.» Find and copy the word that means very brave. | crossed | icy | *fearless | river
test: «Lily stood at the edge of the high cliff, fearless as the wind blew.» What does fearless mean here? | Hungry for lunch | Sleepy | *Not afraid, even in danger | Scared of falling
test: «Ella was scared of the dark, but she walked to the shed to fetch the torch anyway.» What does this show? | She was not brave at all | She was fearless and felt nothing at all | *Real courage: she was afraid, but she did the right thing anyway | She was careless with the torch
exam: «The fearless dog jumped into the cold river to rescue the boy.» What does fearless tell us about the dog? | Lazy | Sleepy | Wet and cold | *Not afraid, and very brave
